00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:03.030 align:start position:0%
 
the realm  do you know what the realm is  it's the thousand blades of aegon's  enemies  a story we agreed to tell each other  over  and over till we forget that it's a lie  what's up ladies and gentlemen welcome  back for another ones of winner update  video  that's right folks george r martin has  given us another update on his not a  blog website  as you all know george r martin is  currently writing the wins of winner  the next book that is slated to be  released in the song of ice and fire  series  this is a book that he has been writing  for nearly a decade  and since i made a wins of winner update  video only a week ago  i typically would not make another one  so fast but this time george r martin  did give us some insight into his  writing schedule  i thought some of you might find this to  be as interesting as i did  it seems as if these updates are  happening more frequently which does  make me want to believe he is almost  done  however i have felt this way for many  many years so who really knows  you know how it is right when we all  start thinking they will announce a  release date  we end up finding out it has been  delayed once again  this is something i discussed in my last  update video  george said the book would be done by  this summer but he recently announced it  would be delayed until next summer  at the very least now the good news is  as of right now he does seem to be  moving along nicely  this is one of the main reasons why he  has given us several updates this summer  so let's have a look at what he said  about the winds of winter yesterday  on his not a blog website george r  martin said i am back in my  fortress of solitude again my isolated  mountain cabin  i'd returned to santa fe for a short  visit to spend some time with paris  deal with some local business that had  piled up during my months away  and of course fulfill my duties to con  zealand the virtual road con  but all that's behind me now and i am  back on the mountain again  which means i am back in westeros again  once more moving ahead with winds of  winter  it is curious how my life has evolved i  mean once upon a time  i actually wrote my books and stories in  the house where i lived  in a home office but some decades ago  wanting more solitude  i bought the house across the street and  made that my writer's retreat  no longer would i write all day in my  red flannel bathrobe  now i would have to dress and put on  shoes and walk all the way across the  street to write  but that worked for a while things  started getting busier though  so busy that i needed a full-time  assistant then the office house had  someone else in it  not just me and my characters and then i  hired a second assistant  and a third and there was more mail more  email  more phone calls and more people coming  by by now  i'm up to five assistants and somewhere  in there i also acquired a movie theater  a bookstore a charitable foundation  investments  a business manager and despite all that  help  i was drowning till i found the mountain  cabin my life up here is very boring  it must be said truth be told i hardly  can be said to have a life  i have one assistant with me at all  times minions i call them  the assistants do two week shifts and  have to stay in quarantine at home  before starting a shift  every morning i wake up and go straight  to the computer where my minions bring  me coffee  i am utterly useless and incoherent  without my morning coffee  and juice and sometimes a light  breakfast then i start to write  sometimes i stay at it until dark other  days i break off in the late afternoon  to answer emails  or return urgent phone calls my  assistant brings me food and drink from  time to time  when i finally break off for the day  usually around sunset  there's dinner then we watch television  or screen a movie  the wi-fi sucks up on the mountain  though so the choices are limited  some nights i read instead i always read  a bit before going to sleep  when a book really grabs hold of me i  may read half the night but that's rare  i sleep the next day i wake up and do  the same  the next day the next day the next day  before covid  i would usually get out once a week or  so to eat at a restaurant  or go to the movies that all ended in  march since then  weeks and months go by when i never  leave the cabin or see another human  being except whoever is on duty that  week  i lose track of what day it is what week  it is what month it is  the time seems to go by very fast it is  now  august and i don't know what happened to  july but it is good for the writing  i wonder if it is the same for other  writers or is it just me  i wonder if i'll ever figure out the  secret of having a life and writing a  book at the very same time  i certainly have not figured it out to  date for the nonce  it is what it is my life is at home on  hold  and i am spending the days in westeros  with my pals mel  and sam and vic and tai and that girl  with no name  over there in braavos well as you can  see  it does sound like he is focused on  finishing this next book  it's a shame he has to isolate himself  in a cabin in the woods just to do so  i think that if he would have focused on  the wins of winner from day one  i'm sure he would have had it done many  years ago but you also have to think  if he did that then he would not be able  to help with any new shows  or write any other books like fire and  blood i think most fans would rather  have the winds of winter before anything  else  but i do understand where george is  coming from sometimes you do actually  get cabin fever  and sometimes you get tired of working  on the same thing over and over again  it can be nice to take a break and focus  on something else especially if you find  yourself having writer's block  you might have to take a step back  re-energize then come back at it  feeling motivated again hopefully george  is able to take advantage of all this  momentum  by actually getting the book done within  the next year it would be amazing if the  winds of winter came out  then was followed up by house of the  dragon that would certainly give us  enough material to discuss for the next  decade while waiting for a dream of  spring  now this is all wishful thinking of  course since george r martin  is isolating himself in a cabin in the  woods there is really no excuse for him  not finishing this book sometime soon  now if i were him i would not even think  about writing one word for the second  volume of fire and blood  until i got the winds of winter done i  think everyone else who is in business  with him would understand  a game of thrones and more specifically  a song of ice and fire is what led to  all these other opportunities  as of right now the winds of winter is  holding him back from finishing his a  song of ice and fire book series  if he can get through that obstacle i  really think it would enhance  all of his other works simply because of  the amount of stress he is under while  trying to finish it but  then again i know nothing all i really  want to say is i am very excited for the  future of this fandom  i mean yeah game of thrones might not  have ended the way we all wanted  but we have yet to see how the creator  of this amazing story wants it to end  based on how incredible his books have  been so far i can only assume the wins  of winner  will take things to the next level as we  reach the climax of the story  house of the dragon is on its way and  the winds of winter will get released  eventually which will bring us one step  closer to  a dream of spring anyways i hope you all  found this update video to be as  interesting as i did  let me know what you think down below as  always i want to thank everyone for  watching the video  and i also want to thank those of you  who support my channel on patreon  i could not do this without you have a  great day everyone  i will see you again very soon bye  [Music]  [Music]  you

